WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.048
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online TOEFL preparation.

2
00:00:05.348 --> 00:00:08.920
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:17.829
Unit sixteen: Speaking: Listen and Repeat. Today you will repeat sentences accurately with clear sounds, stress and rhythm.

4
00:00:18.129 --> 00:00:20.920
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.867 --> 00:00:25.181
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:26.017 --> 00:00:26.878
Repeat.

7
00:00:27.883 --> 00:00:30.173
Repeat means to say again exactly.

8
00:00:30.783 --> 00:00:32.342
Repeat each sentence.

9
00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:35.440
Your turn. Say: Repeat.

10
00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:39.289
Repeat.

11
00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:41.156
Accuracy.

12
00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:45.102
Accuracy means saying exactly the right words.

13
00:00:45.717 --> 00:00:47.356
Accuracy matters most.

14
00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:50.417
Your turn. Say: Accuracy.

15
00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:54.395
Accuracy.

16
00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:55.965
Rhythm.

17
00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:59.809
Rhythm means the pattern of strong and weak sounds.

18
00:01:00.417 --> 00:01:02.138
English has a clear rhythm.

19
00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:05.066
Your turn. Say: Rhythm.

20
00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:08.785
Rhythm.

21
00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:10.539
Stress.

22
00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:14.525
Stress means extra force on a syllable or word.

23
00:01:15.117 --> 00:01:16.698
Put stress on the key word.

24
00:01:17.283 --> 00:01:19.994
Your turn. Say: Stress.

25
00:01:22.833 --> 00:01:23.962
Stress.

26
00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:25.892
Intonation.

27
00:01:26.883 --> 00:01:29.742
Intonation means the rise and fall of the voice.

28
00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:32.106
Use falling intonation.

29
00:01:32.717 --> 00:01:35.601
Your turn. Say: Intonation.

30
00:01:38.467 --> 00:01:39.584
Intonation.

31
00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:41.200
Syllable.

32
00:01:42.217 --> 00:01:44.309
Syllable means a beat in a word.

33
00:01:44.917 --> 00:01:46.754
Banana has three syllables.

34
00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:49.584
Your turn. Say: Syllable.

35
00:01:52.433 --> 00:01:53.411
Syllable.

36
00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:55.267
Visual cue.

37
00:01:56.283 --> 00:01:59.293
Visual cue means a picture that shows the situation.

38
00:01:59.883 --> 00:02:01.233
Use the visual cue.

39
00:02:01.817 --> 00:02:04.841
Your turn. Say: Visual cue.

40
00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:09.142
Visual cue.

41
00:02:09.883 --> 00:02:11.012
Memory chunk.

42
00:02:12.017 --> 00:02:15.293
Memory chunk means a group of words you remember together.

43
00:02:15.883 --> 00:02:18.324
Remember a chunk, not single words.

44
00:02:18.917 --> 00:02:21.732
Your turn. Say: Memory chunk.

45
00:02:24.567 --> 00:02:25.719
Memory chunk.

46
00:02:26.533 --> 00:02:30.312
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:33.196
Visal, what is Listen and Repeat?

48
00:02:34.283 --> 00:02:44.935
You see a picture, hear a short sentence about it and repeat it exactly. You do this for seven sentences, and each one is a little longer than the last.

49
00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:48.038
How can I remember a long sentence?

50
00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:59.198
Remember it in chunks, such as the library opens at nine, and picture the meaning. Say the chunks smoothly instead of word by word.

51
00:03:00.283 --> 00:03:01.923
What does the score depend on?

52
00:03:03.017 --> 00:03:12.914
Accuracy, pronunciation and rhythm. Repeat the sentence clearly without adding words, and keep the stress on the important words.

53
00:03:14.067 --> 00:03:15.741
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:16.583 --> 00:03:21.218
Grammar focus: Strategy: listen in chunks, repeat in rhythm.

55
00:03:21.518 --> 00:03:22.670
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:23.383 --> 00:03:25.615
The library opens at nine o'clock.

57
00:03:26.517 --> 00:03:28.876
Put the stress on the key words, not every word.

58
00:03:29.833 --> 00:03:36.700
Listen to the whole sentence, hold it in chunks, and repeat it with natural stress and rhythm. Do not add or change words.

59
00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:41.879
Be careful! Don't say: I add extra words when I repeat.

60
00:03:43.833 --> 00:03:46.576
Say: I repeat exactly what I hear.

61
00:03:46.876 --> 00:03:48.260
Repeat exactly.

62
00:03:49.067 --> 00:03:51.487
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:53.835
Practising Repetition.

64
00:03:54.135 --> 00:03:56.611
A picture shows students in a library.

65
00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:01.155
The sentence says: The library opens at nine o'clock.

66
00:04:02.167 --> 00:04:06.012
Bopha remembers three chunks: the library, opens, at nine.

67
00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:09.650
She repeats them smoothly with a falling voice.

68
00:04:10.633 --> 00:04:13.573
Her score improves because she keeps the exact words.

69
00:04:14.667 --> 00:04:18.599
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:19.450 --> 00:04:21.368
In this task you repeat blank.

71
00:04:21.668 --> 00:04:26.309
A, a story. B, exactly what you hear. C, your own idea.

72
00:04:29.867 --> 00:04:32.470
The answer is B: exactly what you hear.

73
00:04:33.617 --> 00:04:35.628
How many sentences do you repeat?

74
00:04:35.928 --> 00:04:39.128
A, two. B, fifty. C, seven.

75
00:04:42.667 --> 00:04:44.376
The answer is C: seven.

76
00:04:45.517 --> 00:04:46.982
Chunks help you blank.

77
00:04:47.282 --> 00:04:51.005
A, remember. B, skip words. C, write.

78
00:04:54.567 --> 00:04:56.717
The answer is A: remember.

79
00:04:57.883 --> 00:04:59.360
Which should you not do?

80
00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:03.790
A, use stress. B, add extra words. C, use rhythm.

81
00:05:07.333 --> 00:05:10.320
The answer is B: add extra words.

82
00:05:11.483 --> 00:05:12.949
What does the picture show?

83
00:05:13.249 --> 00:05:17.518
A, a market. B, a beach. C, students in a library.

84
00:05:21.067 --> 00:05:23.809
The answer is C: students in a library.

85
00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:28.186
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:29.050 --> 00:05:31.433
How do you repeat a long sentence correctly?

87
00:05:40.217 --> 00:05:41.636
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:41.936 --> 00:05:55.388
I listen to the whole sentence and remember it in chunks. I think about the meaning, because that helps me remember. Then I repeat it smoothly, with the same stress and rhythm, and I do not add any words.

89
00:05:55.688 --> 00:05:57.409
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:58.317 --> 00:06:03.674
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: listen in chunks, repeat in rhythm.

91
00:06:03.974 --> 00:06:08.995
Today's value is dedication. Practise a little every day, and you will get better.

92
00:06:09.295 --> 00:06:12.040
See you in Unit seventeen. Goodbye!

93
00:06:12.340 --> 00:06:15.643
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

